Description: Playwright browser automation framework with bundled browsers
 Playwright enables reliable end-to-end testing and automation for modern
 web apps. This package ships the playwright npm module (driver and CLI)
 under /usr/lib/node_modules/playwright and the version-pinned Firefox and
 WebKit browser bundles under /usr/lib/ms-playwright. Chromium comes from
 Debian's own chromium package instead of a bundled archive, and is exposed
 to Playwright at the same bundled path it would otherwise use. The Node.js
 runtime is supplied by the consuming image.
 .
 Consumers must set PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/usr/lib/ms-playwright;
 without it Playwright looks in ~/.cache/ms-playwright and every launch
 fails. Parity with upstream's /ms-playwright container path is the
 consuming image's concern (a symlink there, per the package's directory
 layout convention).
 .
 The Depends list is the union of the per-browser Debian 13 library sets
 from upstream's packages/playwright-core/src/server/registry/nativeDeps.ts
 plus its shared font set and the direct DT_NEEDED libraries of the shipped
 binaries, plus Debian's chromium, chromium-common, and chromium-headless-shell
 packages. Display-server
 tooling for headed runs (xvfb) is intentionally left to consumers.
